  "cause": "MuJoCo's time-constant contact parameterisation scales contact stiffness with the effective mass, and at high jaw friction the tangential constraints lock the cube in an unseated multi-contact configuration; the ~440 N stall squeeze is then resolved by distributed 1-5 mm overlaps. Present already for the training-nominal 5 cm / 800 kg/m^3 cube at jaw mu 2.4 (1.6-3.4 mm over placements) and larger for lighter cubes. The grasp is still established and held. Not corrected: removing it requires re-parameterising the validated contact stiffness (excluded by the E5 protocol)."
